  "scope": "Author/editorial intent review, not blind independent review and not owner approval. Each is a compact 16-panel pilot, not a demonstrated 3\u20135 minute episode.",
  "stories": [
    {
      "id": "NG",
      "editorial_strength": "Strongest integration of ambitious city, appealing courier, rescue choice with personal cost and a mysterious next route.",
      "immediate_resolution": "Pell is safe; qualification is missed; personal Lower District letter redirects Aren.",
      "remaining_gap": "Crescent shape and line endpoint vary across actions; final structural repair fixes the largest car/bridge geography break.",
      "owner_decision": "Does Aren\u2019s ambition, frustration and lower-city mystery make you want his next chapter?"
    },
    {
      "id": "BP",
      "editorial_strength": "Clearest emotional mystery: intimate imitation is tempting, fails a precise test, and leaves a real clue without falsely confirming the missing brother.",
      "immediate_resolution": "Neris is freed and the attacking bloom disabled; nursery evidence remains.",
      "remaining_gap": "Root/door geography drifts and the lift-to-turn rule is not perfectly demonstrated.",
      "owner_decision": "Do the elegant menace, restrained banter and nursery investigation earn sustained curiosity?"
    },
    {
      "id": "ST",
      "editorial_strength": "Most immediately legible comic partnership; brute force fails and observation creates a mutually useful agreement.",
      "immediate_resolution": "Bell returned, padding solves sound problem, Tavi earns an independent ride and invitation.",
      "remaining_gap": "Scale and gauntlet-side continuity vary; repaired ending restores the agreed relationship.",
      "owner_decision": "Would you follow Tavi and this ram as a recurring pair, and is this warmth the right tone?"
    },
    {
      "id": "RC",
      "editorial_strength": "Strongest direct power/cost demonstration and brash victory: impact is borrowed, returned, and becomes debt after the reward is won.",
      "immediate_resolution": "Trial cleared and upper-ring key earned; numbness and lender establish future stakes.",
      "remaining_gap": "Black plate switches sides and key becomes a permit briefly; the core exchange reads but exact power bookkeeping is visually inconsistent.",
      "owner_decision": "Do Ren/Vexa rivalry and the price of borrowed force make this progression premise compelling?"
    },
    {
      "id": "FL",
      "editorial_strength": "Most concrete investigative chain and mature lead: a mistaken inference is corrected by visible evidence, then a practical rescue reveals institutional responsibility.",
      "immediate_resolution": "Lio recovered alive, key transferred, siblings safe; Flood Authority becomes next lead.",
      "remaining_gap": "Jaw-bracing contact remains partially unresolved despite repair; memory ripples and glove sides weaken strict rule continuity.",
      "owner_decision": "Would you follow Corin\u2019s supernatural cases and conflict with his former institution?"
    }
  ],
  "cross_series_recommendations": [
    "Keep all five independent and provisional; chapter appeal, character appeal, drawing and power appeal should remain separate choices.",
    "Choose which protagonist relationship and unresolved question earn another chapter before declaring cast or canon.",
    "Retain the quiet-face / tactile clue / wide-world alternation; it gives these short pilots more range than consecutive combat posters.",
    "Future scene planning needs explicit prop ownership and separate current-state contact diagrams at causal pivots. Source-only texture finishing cannot fix a wrong hand, transferred object or impossible prop.",
    "Dialogue is readable and playful, but all five heroes favor dry quick wit. Future writing can distinguish sentence rhythm and emotional restraint further if the owner selects these voices.",
    "Describe this delivery as five compact pilots. The recorded familiar-author checks are evidence of actual inspection, not audience reading-time measurements."
  ],
